  <circle cx="110" cy="30" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="110" y="35" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">A</text>
  <line x1="150" y1="118" x2="170" y2="50" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="175" cy="40" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="175" y="45" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">B</text>
  <line x1="105" y1="230" x2="60" y2="230" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="45" cy="230" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="45" y="235" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">C</text>
  <line x1="280" y1="245" x2="280" y2="210" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <line x1="280" y1="210" x2="330" y2="210" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="345" cy="210" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="345" y="215" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">D</text>
</svg>
<p>Identify the labeled parts A, B, C, and D and choose the correct option:</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Identify the labeled structure A.</strong><br/>Structure A points to the prominent bulged eye situated dorsolaterally on the head, which is covered and protected in water by a transparent nictitating membrane.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Identify the labeled structure B.</strong><br/>Structure B indicates the circular, dark membranous tympanum located postero-lateral to each eye, functioning as an external ear surface to receive sound signals.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Identify the labeled structure C.</strong><br/>Structure C points to the forelimb, which is shorter, non-webbed, and ends in four distinct digits.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Identify the labeled structure D.</strong><br/>Structure D indicates the hindlimb, which is large, highly muscular, and terminates in five webbed digits adapted for swimming and leaping.</p>
<p><strong>Step 5: Final conclusion and conceptual answer.</strong><br/>Assembling the identifications: A corresponds to the eye, B corresponds to the tympanum, C corresponds to the forelimb, and D corresponds to the hindlimb.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A &ndash; Eye, B &ndash; Tympanum, C &ndash; Forelimb, D &ndash; Hindlimb</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A &ndash; Tympanum, B &ndash; Eye, C &ndash; Hindlimb, D &ndash; Forelimb</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A &ndash; Eye, B &ndash; Vocal sac, C &ndash; Forelimb, D &ndash; Hindlimb</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A &ndash; Nostril, B &ndash; Tympanum, C &ndash; Hindlimb, D &ndash; Forelimb</p>]]></text>
    </answer>
