  <ellipse cx="170" cy="200" rx="14" ry="35" fill="#8d6e63" stroke="#4e342e" stroke-width="2"/>
  <ellipse cx="205" cy="200" rx="14" ry="35" fill="#8d6e63" stroke="#4e342e" stroke-width="2"/>
  <path d="M 230 310 L 210 330" fill="none" stroke="#d7ccc8" stroke-width="12" stroke-linecap="round"/>
  <ellipse cx="200" cy="345" rx="16" ry="12" fill="#bcaaa4" stroke="#5d4037" stroke-width="2"/>
  <path d="M 170 355 C 160 365, 180 375, 200 360 C 220 375, 240 365, 230 355 Z" fill="#fff59d" stroke="#fbc02d" stroke-width="2"/>
  <line x1="160" y1="101" x2="110" y2="50" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="95" cy="45" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="95" y="50" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">A</text>
  <line x1="270" y1="180" x2="350" y2="180" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="365" cy="180" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="365" y="185" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">B</text>
  <line x1="285" y1="285" x2="350" y2="285" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="365" cy="285" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="365" y="290" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">C</text>
  <line x1="185" y1="345" x2="110" y2="345" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="95" cy="345" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="95" y="350" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">D</text>
</svg>
<p>Choose the option that correctly identifies the labeled structures A, B, C, and D:</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Identify structure A.</strong><br/>Structure A is a distinct greenish sac-like organ nestled beneath the lobes of the liver; it represents the gall bladder, which stores the bile secreted by the liver.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Identify structure B.</strong><br/>Structure B is the elongated, curved, wide muscular chamber of the alimentary canal receiving food from the oesophagus; it represents the stomach, where gastric juice and hydrochloric acid initiate chemical digestion to produce chyme.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Identify structure C.</strong><br/>Structure C represents the coiled tubular section that succeeds the stomach, receives pancreatic juice and bile via the common bile duct, and carries out final digestion and nutrient absorption via villi and microvilli; it is the small intestine.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Identify structure D.</strong><br/>Structure D represents the terminal dilated chamber where the rectum and urinogenital ducts terminate; it is the cloaca, which opens to the outside via the cloacal aperture.</p>
<p><strong>Step 5: Final conclusion and conceptual answer.</strong><br/>The correct sequence of identifications is: A represents the gall bladder, B represents the stomach, C represents the intestine, and D represents the cloaca.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
