  <text x="45" y="95" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">A</text>
  <line x1="150" y1="102" x2="190" y2="60" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="195" cy="48" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="195" y="53" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">B</text>
  <line x1="268" y1="240" x2="340" y2="240" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="355" cy="240" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="355" y="245" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">C</text>
  <line x1="248" y1="300" x2="340" y2="300" stroke="#c62828" stroke-width="2"/>
  <circle cx="355" cy="300" r="14" fill="#c62828"/>
  <text x="355" y="305" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="bold" fill="#ffffff" text-anchor="middle">D</text>
</svg>
<p>Select the option that correctly identifies the labeled structures A, B, C, and D:</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Step 1: Identify structure A.</strong><br/>Structure A designates the yellowish ovoid gonad attached to the upper part of each kidney by a double peritoneal fold known as the mesorchium; this organ is the testis.</p>
<p><strong>Step 2: Identify structure B.</strong><br/>Structure B marks the fine, slender ductules (10 to 12 in number) arising from each testis that enter the medial border of the kidney to open into Bidder's canal; these are the vasa efferentia.</p>
<p><strong>Step 3: Identify structure C.</strong><br/>Structure C indicates the duct emerging posteriorly from the kidney of a male frog; because it transmits both urine from the kidneys and spermatozoa from Bidder's canal, it functions as a urinogenital duct.</p>
<p><strong>Step 4: Identify structure D.</strong><br/>Structure D represents the median dilated chamber that receives the urinogenital ducts, rectum, and urinary bladder before communicating with the exterior; it is the cloaca.</p>
<p><strong>Step 5: Final conclusion and conceptual answer.</strong><br/>The correct identification sequence is: A represents the testis, B represents the vasa efferentia, C represents the urinogenital duct, and D represents the cloaca.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
